WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.222
It was a normal November morning—except for one thing.

2
00:00:07.223 --> 00:00:10.263
Everyone was upset about something.

3
00:00:10.264 --> 00:00:13.832
My brother, Tate, was upset because of me.

4
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:16.803
"Mom!" Tate yelled.

5
00:00:16.804 --> 00:00:20.636
"I found more of Iggy's junk in my closet!"

6
00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:24.308
I had moved into my own room a while ago.

7
00:00:24.309 --> 00:00:27.439
I guess I'd left some stuff behind.

8
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.216
"Tell him to get it out of here!" Tate complained.

9
00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:34.789
My mom walked into my room.

10
00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:40.527
"Iggy, please clean your stuff out of Tate's closet today after school," she said.

11
00:00:40.528 --> 00:00:44.697
Suddenly she looked around my room.

12
00:00:44.698 --> 00:00:47.477
Then she got upset.

13
00:00:47.478 --> 00:00:51.585
"And clean your own room, Iggy!" she added.

14
00:00:51.586 --> 00:00:53.760
"It's a mess!"

15
00:00:53.761 --> 00:00:56.355
Of course my room is a mess.

16
00:00:56.356 --> 00:01:00.428
It's the room of a brilliant inventor—me, Iggy!

17
00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:03.672
Brilliant people always have messy rooms.

18
00:01:03.673 --> 00:01:09.467
I bet Thomas Edison, who invented the light bulb, had a super messy room.

19
00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:12.874
And I bet his mom didn't tell him to clean it up!

20
00:01:12.875 --> 00:01:18.881
She probably knew that he was busy thinking up clever new inventions, just like me.

21
00:01:18.882 --> 00:01:23.699
That morning I walked to school with my friends Molly, Josh, and Jenny.

22
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.391
And Molly was upset too.

23
00:01:26.392 --> 00:01:29.399
She told us why as we walked along.

24
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.387
"My mom hired a babysitter for Caswell and me," she said.

25
00:01:34.388 --> 00:01:38.166
"Mom wanted some time to meet a friend or go shopping."

26
00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.425
"That's great," I said.

27
00:01:40.426 --> 00:01:44.495
"Meeting a friend always puts my mom in a good mood."

28
00:01:44.496 --> 00:01:48.030
"But you don't understand," said Molly.

29
00:01:48.031 --> 00:01:51.615
"I don't like Lucy, our new babysitter."

30
00:01:51.616 --> 00:01:56.764
"Is she mean, like a wicked stepmother?" asked Jenny.

31
00:01:56.765 --> 00:02:00.276
Jenny's class was reading fairy tales.

32
00:02:00.277 --> 00:02:04.346
Fairy tales have lots of wicked stepmothers in them.

33
00:02:04.347 --> 00:02:08.249
"No, Lucy is not mean," said Molly.

34
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:12.822
"Why don't you like her then?" asked Josh.

35
00:02:12.823 --> 00:02:16.893
"Well," said Molly, "she talks on her cell phone a lot. And

36
00:02:16.894 --> 00:02:22.715
she and Caswell watch the TV show Monster Madness every day." "That

37
00:02:22.716 --> 00:02:25.593
sounds like fun," I said. "My

38
00:02:25.594 --> 00:02:30.723
mom won't let Tate and me watch any TV after school." "

39
00:02:30.724 --> 00:02:35.775
Monster Madness is a pretty scary show," said Molly.

40
00:02:35.776 --> 00:02:40.265
"Even when I'm in my room, I can still hear the monsters roaring.

41
00:02:40.266 --> 00:02:44.333
Now I can't sleep at night!"

42
00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:50.038
"Why don't you just ask Lucy if you can watch something else?" I said.

43
00:02:50.039 --> 00:02:53.167
"No way!" Molly replied.

44
00:02:53.168 --> 00:02:56.222
"Lucy and Caswell would think I'm a big baby.

45
00:02:56.223 --> 00:03:02.195
Caswell is much younger than I am, and he's not scared at all!"

46
00:03:02.196 --> 00:03:09.712
That morning Molly yawned at least ten times during social studies.

47
00:03:09.713 --> 00:03:13.622
"Molly," said our teacher, Mrs. Romano.

48
00:03:13.623 --> 00:03:17.680
"What did Egyptian children do in their spare time?"

49
00:03:17.681 --> 00:03:24.331
"Sleep?" said Molly, yawning again.

50
00:03:24.332 --> 00:03:30.588
Everyone laughed, except for Mrs. Romano and me.

51
00:03:30.589 --> 00:03:34.829
Mrs. Romano seemed annoyed that Molly wasn't paying attention.

52
00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:39.164
And I was a little worried about our language arts project.

53
00:03:39.165 --> 00:03:43.086
Soon we were going to start writing books.

54
00:03:43.087 --> 00:03:49.695
Molly and I were partners, so I needed her to be alert and wide-awake.

55
00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:54.343
On the way home after school we passed Bubbles Bath Shop.

56
00:03:54.344 --> 00:03:58.812
Josh and Jenny's dad had recently gotten a job there.

57
00:03:58.813 --> 00:04:01.232
We stopped and looked in the window.

58
00:04:01.233 --> 00:04:06.762
A sign read "Bathe Your Worries Away In A Relaxing Bubble Bath!"

59
00:04:06.763 --> 00:04:13.496
"Bubbles Bath Shop sells lots of different kinds of bubble bath soap," said Jenny.

60
00:04:13.497 --> 00:04:18.286
"Chocolate, strawberry, and even bubble gum," added Josh.

61
00:04:18.287 --> 00:04:22.660
Suddenly I got an idea for a new invention.

62
00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:27.344
It was an invention that would help Molly relax.

63
00:04:27.345 --> 00:04:31.830
It might also keep my mom and Tate from getting upset with me.

64
00:04:31.831 --> 00:04:39.603
Now that would really be a great invention!

